course: dictionary
lesson: 6672
title: Obedient
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Obedient means doing what you are told. It describes someone, or an animal, that follows orders from a parent, teacher, rule or owner. An obedient dog sits when its owner says sit.
explain: «Yes, I am too wise for this play; but see that you make all the Animals obedient to me.» The Man wants the animals to do what he tells them. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Something like "doing what they are told" fits, so obedient must mean that.
explain: Being obedient is often good, but stories also ask when it is right to say no. «I will never be obedient to this son of Adam» shows the crab refusing to follow the man's orders. If someone asks you to do something wrong or unsafe, saying no can be the right choice.
fact: Obedient means doing what you are told by a parent, teacher, rule or owner.
fact: Animals can be obedient too: an obedient dog is trained to follow commands.
fact: The word is an adjective, and its comparative form is more obedient.
fact: «Obedient» can describe a machine: «a computer is incredibly fast and incredibly obedient» means it does exactly what it is told.
fact: In church life, obedience to God is one of the monastic vows.
exercise: «A computer is incredibly fast and incredibly obedient.» What does obedient mean here? | Sings songs when it is bored | *Does exactly what it is told | Makes its own rules | Is very slow
exercise: Pau Amma the Crab says, «I will never be obedient to this son of Adam.» What is the crab saying? | *It will refuse to follow the man's orders | It will do whatever the man asks | It will go to sleep | It will ask the man for help
exercise: Which of these is most like an obedient dog? | A dog that chases every cat | A dog that never comes inside | *A dog that sits and stays when its owner says so | A dog that buries bones in the garden
test: Ravi always does what his teacher asks, even when the task is hard. Which word describes him? | Careless | *Obedient | Loud | Curious
test: Which is the best meaning of obedient? | Being very tall | Telling jokes to everyone | Running very fast | *Doing what you are told
exam: Which is a time it might be right not to be obedient? | Your parent asks you to tidy your room | *Someone asks you to do something wrong or unsafe | Your friend asks you to share a book | Your teacher asks you to sit down
